# ═══ Draft knowledge entry — published autotools dep .la carries stale third-party
# .la absolute path (old prefix) in dependency_libs; fix by sed-deleting the dead ref
# and injecting all dep -l at the end of LIBS
# Software: libfreefare 0.4.0
# Gate: conan-verify G2 (conan create, ohos-aarch64-fixed) + test_package 1/1 + W3
# Status: DRAFT

id: libfreefare-0.4.0-published-la-stale-thirdparty-abs-path
severity: 3
category: build-system|libtool|linking|ohos
trigger_tool: configure|make|libtool|conan
phase: link

keywords: libtool, .la, dependency_libs, stale prefix, /usr/local/lib, not a valid libtool archive, undefined symbol, libusb, LIBS, autotools
error_signature: not a valid libtool archive|/usr/local/lib/.*\.la|undefined symbol: libusb_|is not a valid libtool archive
match_keywords: libnfc.la, libusb-1.0.la, dependency_libs, absolute path, HMDFS, examples, undefined symbol, LIBS

root_cause: |
  (1) A published autotools dependency (libnfc/1.8.0) was built under prefix=/usr/local,
  so its lib/libnfc.la dependency_libs line hardcodes the absolute path
  /usr/local/lib/libusb-1.0.la (the libtool chain record of libusb-compat -> libusb-1.0).
  On the OHOS device this absolute path does not exist (libusb-1.0 actually lives under a
  conan-cache hash dir), so libtool sed-resolving dependency_libs hits a non-existent .la
  and aborts with "is not a valid libtool archive".
  (2) Separately, examples/ link fails with undefined symbol: libusb_* because
  libusb-compat (the 0.1 shim) references libusb-1.0, but the default LIBS only carries
  -lusb, not -lusb-1.0; and -lusb-1.0 must come AFTER -lusb to resolve symbols.
  AutotoolsToolchain does not append every dependency's -l to LIBS.

rec_approach: sed-dead-la-ref + inject-all-dep-libs-at-end
rec_description: |
  (1) Unlike DRAFT-ohos-la-libdir-hardcode (libdir='//lib', fix = copy .la to a staging dir
  and inject -L staging into configure LDFLAGS), here the dead reference is a SINGLE third-party
  .la absolute path while the actual library is still reachable via -L<pkg libdir> -lusb.
  So the lighter fix is to sed-delete just that absolute .la token from the dependency's .la
  in build() before configure:
      sed 's# /usr/local/lib/libusb-1.0.la##g' <dep>/lib/libnfc.la
  Keep the -L<dir> -lusb entries so libtool still resolves the real library.
  (2) In generate() (BEFORE configure, so it is baked into the Makefile; doing it in build()
  after configure has no effect), append EVERY dependency's -l to LIBS:
      for dep in self.dependencies.values():
          for lib in dep.cpp_info.libs:
              env.append("LIBS", "-l" + lib)
      env.append("LIBS", "-lcrypto")   # openssl not picked up by PKG_CHECK_MODULES
  This guarantees libusb-compat -> libusb-1.0 -> libcrypto symbol order.
  (3) Decision rule vs the staging recipe: if the dead .la reference can be backstopped by
  -L<actual dir> -l<name>, sed-delete it; only copy-and-rewrite-to-staging when the whole
  .la chain (libdir field itself) is wrong.

rec_commands:
  - "sed 's# /usr/local/lib/libusb-1.0.la##g' $CONAN_LIB/libnfc.la"
  - "generate(): for dep in self.dependencies.values(): for lib in dep.cpp_info.libs: env.append('LIBS','-l'+lib)"

verification: |
  conan create on ohos-aarch64-fixed (clang 15) rc=0; libfreefare.la and all 13 bin/mifare-*
  link; test_package 1/1 Passed (11 hardware-free assertions on sector geometry / AID / keys / MAD / TLV).

related:
  - knowledge/drafts/DRAFT-ohos-la-libdir-hardcode.md (//lib libdir hardcode, staging recipe)
  - archives/l/libfreefare/0.4.0/notes.md (full device pit table, 9 issues)
last_updated: 2026-09-23
